1
00:00:00,054 --> 00:00:02,109
Kao died in Delhi on January 20,

2
00:00:02,576 --> 00:00:03,424
2002.

3
00:00:03,772 --> 00:00:04,641
He was eighty-three.

4
00:00:04,958 --> 00:00:06,262
He never wrote a memoir.

5
00:00:06,609 --> 00:00:08,217
He almost never gave interviews.

6
00:00:08,554 --> 00:00:10,261
He avoided cameras, even at family

7
00:00:10,272 --> 00:00:10,750
weddings.

8
00:00:11,834 --> 00:00:14,073
Some of his papers remain restricted, on

9
00:00:14,084 --> 00:00:15,204
his own instructions.

10
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:18,476
Abroad, his peers knew exactly who he was.

11
00:00:18,823 --> 00:00:20,215
The head of French intelligence,

12
00:00:20,508 --> 00:00:22,541
Alexandre de Marenches, was quoted

13
00:00:22,552 --> 00:00:25,160
admiring "a fascinating mix of physical

14
00:00:25,171 --> 00:00:26,171
and mental elegance."

15
00:00:26,504 --> 00:00:26,993
At home?

16
00:00:28,038 --> 00:00:28,821
Almost nothing.

17
00:00:29,169 --> 00:00:31,104
His first full biography, by

18
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:34,060
Nitin Gokhale, appeared only in 2019.

19
00:00:34,408 --> 00:00:36,441
That was seventeen years after his death.

20
00:00:37,424 --> 00:00:40,283
Today R&AW holds a memorial lecture in his

21
00:00:40,294 --> 00:00:41,185
name every year.

22
00:00:42,281 --> 00:00:44,509
The most famous Indian spy is still a man

23
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:46,314
most Indians would not recognise.

